  "description": "Intracranial EEG segments from five epilepsy patients, repackaged in BIDS from the Bonn dataset of Andrzejak et al. (2001). The release includes sets C and D (seizure-free interictal recordings from the hippocampal formation and the epileptogenic zone) and set E (ictal activity), with 100 single-channel segments of 23.6 s per set. The data were converted losslessly to BrainVision format, and every sample is identical to the source text files. Scalp EEG sets A and B are excluded.",
  "methods_description": "Segments were cut from continuous multichannel presurgical depth and strip electrode EEG recordings. Recordings used a 128-channel amplifier with an average common reference, 12-bit analog-to-digital conversion, and a sampling rate of 173.61 Hz. Segments were selected after visual artifact inspection and a weak-stationarity criterion. Each segment is 23.6 s long and contains 4097 samples. Conversion from ASCII to BrainVision INT_16 involved no filtering, resampling, re-referencing or rescaling.",
